    2026 Oct 19 21:43:21 user.notice awplus NSM[946]: port1.0.16 user no shutdown
    2026 Oct 19 21:43:21 user.notice awplus NSM[946]: Port up notification received for port1.0.16

  The DUT detected and logged all four link transitions, in exactly the same words: two for the
  armed port and two for the unarmed port.  It sent a trap for two of them.

  Correlation with the wire, applying the measured 15 s skew (the DUT is behind the box):
  21:41:38 -> box 10:41:53 against trap #1 at 10:41:52.459; 21:42:10 -> box 10:42:25 against
  trap #2 at 10:42:23.920.  Both agree within about one second.  That is the resolution of a
  log stamped to the second compared against a capture stamped to the millisecond.

  The RSTP churn is in the log too, and it is what STEP 1 predicted.  The root port moved from
  port1.0.2 to port1.0.16 when the root port went down, and moved back when it returned.
  => STEP 5 PASS: `snmp trap link-status` gates the NOTIFICATION, not the detection.  The
     silence for port1.0.16 is the feature working.  It is not a stimulus that failed.  This
     is what turns the STEP 4 control into a measurement.

