STEP 8 -- designed: persistence across a reboot                               NOT RUN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  This case performed no reload and wrote nothing to startup-config.  Persistence of
  `snmp trap link-status` across a reboot is NOT MEASURED, and it is claimed nowhere in this
  log.  The reason is the bench, not a choice about this case.  The layer 3 addresses this
  case needs -- `interface vlan10 10.38.22.34/27` on port1.0.10 -- exist in running-config
  only.  The boot config is `flash:/default.cfg`, and it does not contain them.  A reload
  would therefore destroy the path to the trap receiver.  Writing those addresses to
  startup-config would change the standing bench, which is never done unattended.
  => STEP 8 NOT RUN: a reload cannot be done on this bench without changing the standing
     configuration of the box.  Reboot persistence is left unmeasured.
